ab-tests/shop-now.abtest.ts:11:phone:visreg:<28.2s> Loading every test page on both the control server and the experiment server, taking a screenshot of each once the page has settled, and comparing the two screenshots pixel-by-pixel. A test fails when the two sides look visibly different. This is how a code change that does not break anything functionally still gets caught when it accidentally moves a button, shifts a layout, or changes a color.
